# MyFileSync agent rules

## Scope

- This repo is **MyFileSync** — a standalone Windows-first folder sync/backup app (Electron + React).
- **Do not** reference, import, copy from, or depend on **MyFileExplorer**, **BackupMirror** source, or any other project.
- Canonical plan: `PLAN.md`. Specs: `docs/`. Implement against those files only.
- Legacy **BackupMirror** behavior may be referenced from specs for parity; reimplement in this repo.

## Architecture

- Electron **main** owns compare/sync engine, Win32 ADS, SQLite, job files.
- Renderer is React + Zustand; **no Node integration**.
- Typed preload IPC + Zod; Result envelope `{ ok, value } | { ok: false, error }`.
- App state under Electron `userData` — job JSON, sync DB, logs, settings.

## ADS (core differentiator)

- NTFS→NTFS: use **CopyFileEx** / **CopyFileW** or explicit **copyStreams** — never `$DATA`-only stream pipe for large files.
- Compare and sync **alternate stream manifests** (name + size; optional hash).
- Optional compare cache in file ADS (`MD5`, folder stats) is **per-job opt-in** (`ads.writeCacheToAds`).
- Plain-language errors for read-only folders and permission denied — not raw EPERM.

## Safety

- Validate/normalize all paths in main before IO.
- Recycle Bin default for sync deletes (D6).
- Mirror with deletes requires user confirm when delete count &gt; 0.
- Do not browse or exfiltrate user disks beyond what the task requires.

## Settings and jobs

- Every new job field must be added to **`jobSchema`** (Zod) so export/import round-trips.
- Do not invent parallel export allowlists for job preferences.

## Specs vs code

- Until scaffold exists, prefer updating `docs/` + `PLAN.md` when product decisions change.
- Keep [docs/DECISIONS.md](docs/DECISIONS.md) in sync when locking behavior.

## Tests

- Pure compare/ADS path logic in `shared/` — unit test with Vitest.
- Win32 integration tests manual or Windows CI only.
